# Upstream: giac 2.1.0 sym2poly.cc algnum_convert (normal and simplify of an expression with algebraic numbers): it rewrites each rootof(p,pmin) as p evaluated at the generator rootof(pmin), but only the rootofs that lvar(e) lists at the top level (sym2poly.cc:4581-4587). A rootof inside a power, sqrt(rootof([1,1],P)), stays, and the loop below writes the base of the power with V -> VARS (sym2poly.cc:4685, "DOIT base should be reduced wrt syst"), where the rootof's variable stands for the generator (sym2poly.cc:4668 adds the numerator p to E only): the base lost its numerator polynomial, so normal(sqrt(rootof([1,1],P))) was the square root of the generator. normal and simplify reach it for any square root over a field Giac writes as a rootof: normal(sqrt(1+sqrt(1+2^(1/3)))) was rootof([[1,0],[-1,0,0,0,3,0,4,0,15,0,24,0,5]])/227 = 0.00732288514727 (mpmath 1.58218310546), the same rootof for sqrt(2+sqrt(1+2^(1/3))) and sqrt(2*sqrt(1+2^(1/3))), also with 3^(1/3) and 2^(1/4) inside (backlog F228). Now every rootof of e is rewritten (lop, which also finds those inside a power or a function), so the base holds p(generator). The answer is still a rootof (of the root's primitive element, with larger coefficients), now with the right value. G340f1: the rewrite wrote the generator as the one-argument rootof(pmin) (sym2poly.cc:4592-4593), a form Giac's own rootof() never gives (alg_ext.cc:1359 makes it rootof([1,0],pmin)); a rootof([1,0],P) under a power, left as it was before this patch, became rootof(P); the power branch's _factors(x^2-rootof(P)) (sym2poly.cc:4692) split it, so the root's value was set to 1 (:4712) and its equation to x2-1, and normal(sqrt(2^(1/3)+3^(1/3))), simplify(sqrt(2^(1/3)+sqrt(3))) and normal(sqrt(3^(1/3)+7^(1/3))) gave 1 (mpmath 1.64382803851, 1.72973172991, 1.83171524891; stock right). The generator is now rootof([1,0],pmin).
# Changed by Pascaline contributors, 2026-11-12
--- a/src/sym2poly.cc
+++ b/src/sym2poly.cc
@@ -4581,16 +4581,22 @@
     v=lvar(e);
     vecteur vr,wr;
     // rewrite rootofs inside e
-    for (int i=0;i<v.size();++i){
-      if (v[i].is_symb_of_sommet(at_rootof)){
-        gen f=v[i]._SYMBptr->feuille;
+    // N62 patch 0045 (G340): every rootof of e, also one inside a power or a function (lop, where lvar lists the power
+    // itself): the base of a power is written below in terms of the generator's variable, so a rootof left inside it
+    // lost its numerator polynomial (normal(sqrt(rootof([1,1],P))) was the root of the generator)
+    vecteur lr=lop(e,at_rootof);
+    for (int i=0;i<lr.size();++i){
+      if (lr[i].is_symb_of_sommet(at_rootof)){
+        gen f=lr[i]._SYMBptr->feuille;
         if (f.type==_VECT && f._VECTptr->size()==2){
-          vr.push_back(v[i]);
+          vr.push_back(lr[i]);
           gen p=f._VECTptr->front(),pmin=f._VECTptr->back();
           if (p.type==_VECT && pmin.type==_VECT && p._VECTptr->size()>=pmin._VECTptr->size())
             p=p%pmin;
-          pmin.subtype=_POLY1__VECT;
-          wr.push_back(horner(p,symbolic(at_rootof,pmin)));
+          // N62 patch 0045 (G340f1): the generator as rootof([1,0],pmin), the form Giac's rootof() gives (alg_ext.cc rootof);
+          // with the one-argument rootof(pmin) written here before, _factors in the power branch below split x^2-rootof(pmin)
+          // and set the root to 1: normal(sqrt(rootof([1,0],P))) for the degree-6 P of 2^(1/3)+sqrt(3) gave 1
+          wr.push_back(horner(p,symbolic(at_rootof,makevecteur(makevecteur(1,0),pmin))));
         }
       }
     }
